	/// Voluntary departures relative to average daily workforce. Calculation: Voluntary Exits / Average Daily Headcount. Purpose: Isolates voluntary turnover while retaining the full workforce exposure denominator. Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place. Date/filter context: Numerator follows active Exit Date; denominator counts lifecycle-active employees on every day of the selected min/max interval, capped at global payroll coverage. Department and employee filters apply to both populations. Empty/zero behavior: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Limitations: Period rate, not annualized; zero or BLANK denominator returns BLANK. Interpretation: Higher indicates more voluntary turnover over the selected interval.
	measure 'Voluntary Attrition Rate' =
			// Voluntary departures relative to average daily workforce.
			// Why: Isolates voluntary turnover while retaining the full workforce exposure denominator.
			// Logic: Voluntary Exits / Average Daily Headcount.
			// Context: Numerator follows active Exit Date; denominator counts lifecycle-active employees on every day of the selected min/max interval, capped at global payroll coverage. Department and employee filters apply to both populations.
			// Empty/zero: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied.
			// Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place.
			// Caveat: Period rate, not annualized; zero or BLANK denominator returns BLANK.
			DIVIDE([Voluntary Exits],[Average Daily Headcount])
		formatString: 0.0%
		displayFolder: 02 Retention
		lineageTag: b29aa474-00c8-403d-b60a-5935d390e99c

