	/// Mean completed employment tenure among selected exit events. Calculation: For each Exit row, days from related Employee Hire Date to Exit Date / 365.25, averaged over exit rows. Purpose: Uses the linked hire date to describe when selected employees leave in their employment lifecycle. Unit: Years, using elapsed days / 365.25. Date/filter context: Active Exit Date selects exit events; related Employee Hire Date supplies tenure start. Department and employee filters apply. This measure has no explicit payroll coverage cap. Empty/zero behavior: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Averages ignore BLANK values; a mean without qualifying observations is BLANK unless zero is explicitly supplied. Limitations: Exit Date filters events; employee/department filters also apply. Years use a 365.25-day convention. Interpretation: Shorter tenure can indicate early attrition; it does not by itself establish its cause.
	measure 'Average Exit Tenure Years' =
			// Mean completed employment tenure among selected exit events.
			// Why: Uses the linked hire date to describe when selected employees leave in their employment lifecycle.
			// Logic: For each Exit row, days from related Employee Hire Date to Exit Date / 365.25, averaged over exit rows.
			// Context: Active Exit Date selects exit events; related Employee Hire Date supplies tenure start. Department and employee filters apply. This measure has no explicit payroll coverage cap.
			// Empty/zero: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Averages ignore BLANK values; a mean without qualifying observations is BLANK unless zero is explicitly supplied.
			// Unit: Years, using elapsed days / 365.25.
			// Caveat: Exit Date filters events; employee/department filters also apply. Years use a 365.25-day convention.
			AVERAGEX('Fact_Exit',DIVIDE(DATEDIFF(RELATED('Dim_Employee'[Hire Date]),'Fact_Exit'[Exit Date],DAY),365.25))
		formatString: 0.0
		displayFolder: 02 Retention
		lineageTag: d9d7bbc8-9afa-4ffc-b0ed-3bbac355c8de

	/// Mean employment tenure of employees active at the selected endpoint. Calculation: Filter employees by lifecycle-active dates; average days from Hire Date to endpoint / 365.25. Purpose: Calculates tenure at the requested endpoint instead of using the fixed extract Tenure Band. Unit: Years, using elapsed days / 365.25. Date/filter context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications. Empty/zero behavior: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Averages ignore BLANK values; a mean without qualifying observations is BLANK unless zero is explicitly supplied. Limitations: No explicit future-only guard in this expression: it uses the capped endpoint even if selected start is later. Preserve this existing behavior. Interpretation: Describes experience in the active cohort; a larger value is not automatically better.
	measure 'Average Active Tenure Years' =
			// Mean employment tenure of employees active at the selected endpoint.
			// Why: Calculates tenure at the requested endpoint instead of using the fixed extract Tenure Band.
			// Logic: Filter employees by lifecycle-active dates; average days from Hire Date to endpoint / 365.25.
			// Context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications.
			// Empty/zero: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Averages ignore BLANK values; a mean without qualifying observations is BLANK unless zero is explicitly supplied.
			// Unit: Years, using elapsed days / 365.25.
			// Caveat: No explicit future-only guard in this expression: it uses the capped endpoint even if selected start is later. Preserve this existing behavior.
			VAR _d=[Period End Date] RETURN AVERAGEX(FILTER('Dim_Employee','Dim_Employee'[Hire Date]<=_d && (ISBLANK('Dim_Employee'[Exit Date]) || 'Dim_Employee'[Exit Date]>_d)),DIVIDE(DATEDIFF('Dim_Employee'[Hire Date],_d,DAY),365.25))
		formatString: 0.0
		displayFolder: 01 Workforce
		lineageTag: 367cf008-2fea-466e-a28c-dabe94fba277

