	/// Share of the selected active workforce in the source Female category. Calculation: Female Headcount / Active Headcount As Of Date. Purpose: Normalizes composition for the size of the filtered population. Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place. Date/filter context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications. Empty/zero behavior: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Limitations: An existing Gender slicer also filters the denominator; selecting Female alone therefore yields 100% when nonempty. Zero denominator returns BLANK. Interpretation: Read as population composition, not a performance score or inferred gender identity.
	measure 'Female Workforce Share' =
			// Share of the selected active workforce in the source Female category.
			// Why: Normalizes composition for the size of the filtered population.
			// Logic: Female Headcount / Active Headcount As Of Date.
			// Context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications.
			// Empty/zero: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied.
			// Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place.
			// Caveat: An existing Gender slicer also filters the denominator; selecting Female alone therefore yields 100% when nonempty. Zero denominator returns BLANK.
			DIVIDE([Female Headcount],[Active Headcount As Of Date])
		formatString: 0.0%
