	/// Active headcount share after removing the explicit department table and employee department-name filters. Calculation: Active Headcount / Active Headcount recalculated without Dim_Department filters and without Dim_Employee[Department] filters. Purpose: Shows relative departmental workforce scale while preserving other employee selections. Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place. Date/filter context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications. Empty/zero behavior: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Limitations: Other Employee attributes, including any separate employee department-key filter, remain. Denominator is not ALLSELECTED departments; zero denominator returns BLANK. Interpretation: A larger value means a larger share of the otherwise selected workforce.
	measure 'Department Headcount Share' =
			// Active headcount share after removing the explicit department table and employee department-name filters.
			// Why: Shows relative departmental workforce scale while preserving other employee selections.
			// Logic: Active Headcount / Active Headcount recalculated without Dim_Department filters and without Dim_Employee[Department] filters.
			// Context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications.
			// Empty/zero: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied.
			// Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place.
			// Caveat: Other Employee attributes, including any separate employee department-key filter, remain. Denominator is not ALLSELECTED departments; zero denominator returns BLANK.
			DIVIDE([Active Headcount As Of Date],CALCULATE([Active Headcount As Of Date],REMOVEFILTERS('Dim_Department'),REMOVEFILTERS('Dim_Employee'[Department])))
		formatString: 0.0%
		displayFolder: 01 Workforce
		lineageTag: 3d7e87d4-7f34-49d3-86e6-efc9fd3e0d1c

	/// Dense descending headcount rank among selected departments. Calculation: When Department is in scope, RANKX over ALLSELECTED Department using Active Headcount; otherwise BLANK. Purpose: Supports comparison within the visible department selection and avoids meaningless grand-total ranks. Unit: Dense ordinal rank; 1 is highest headcount. Date/filter context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications. Empty/zero behavior: Explicit BLANK guards and suppressed totals are retained exactly as written. Limitations: Ranks only in a Department grouping; total/card contexts return BLANK. Current job/demographic filters remain active. Interpretation: 1 is the largest active workforce; ties share a rank.
	measure 'Department Headcount Rank' =
			// Dense descending headcount rank among selected departments.
			// Why: Supports comparison within the visible department selection and avoids meaningless grand-total ranks.
			// Logic: When Department is in scope, RANKX over ALLSELECTED Department using Active Headcount; otherwise BLANK.
			// Context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications.
			// Empty/zero: Explicit BLANK guards and suppressed totals are retained exactly as written.
			// Unit: Dense ordinal rank; 1 is highest headcount.
			// Caveat: Ranks only in a Department grouping; total/card contexts return BLANK. Current job/demographic filters remain active.
			IF(ISINSCOPE('Dim_Department'[Department]),RANKX(ALLSELECTED('Dim_Department'[Department]),[Active Headcount As Of Date],,DESC,Dense),BLANK())
		formatString: #,##0
		displayFolder: 01 Workforce
		lineageTag: 6aa772a7-d1e7-4621-b452-56f492924391

	/// Average current extract annual salary of lifecycle-active employees at the capped endpoint. Calculation: Average Employee Annual Salary across employees passing hire/exit lifecycle eligibility. Purpose: Uses one salary per active employee rather than transaction-weighted payroll. Unit: Unspecified source monetary units. Date/filter context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications. Empty/zero behavior: Averages ignore BLANK values; a mean without qualifying observations is BLANK unless zero is explicitly supplied. Limitations: Historical salary changes and FX/currency policy are unavailable. Expression has no explicit future-only start guard. Interpretation: Annual compensation level in unspecified source currency units; compare only under a consistent currency interpretation.
	measure 'Average Annual Salary' =
			// Average current extract annual salary of lifecycle-active employees at the capped endpoint.
