	/// Share of recorded employee-days showing presence, lateness or half-day attendance. Calculation: (Present Records + Late Records + Half Day Records) / Attendance Records. Purpose: Uses only observable records rather than assuming a schedule. Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place. Date/filter context: Active Attendance Date and Department/Employee filters select recorded employee-days. Latest source observation is 27 June 2025; unrecorded dates are not inferred absent. Empty/zero behavior: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Limitations: Half-Day counts as one presence record. Leave and Absent remain in denominator. Not scheduled attendance or FTE-weighted attendance; zero denominator returns BLANK. Interpretation: Higher means a larger observed presence share; assess late and half-day components separately.
	measure 'Recorded Attendance Rate' =
			// Share of recorded employee-days showing presence, lateness or half-day attendance.
			// Why: Uses only observable records rather than assuming a schedule.
			// Logic: (Present Records + Late Records + Half Day Records) / Attendance Records.
			// Context: Active Attendance Date and Department/Employee filters select recorded employee-days. Latest source observation is 27 June 2025; unrecorded dates are not inferred absent.
			// Empty/zero: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied.
			// Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place.
			// Caveat: Half-Day counts as one presence record. Leave and Absent remain in denominator. Not scheduled attendance or FTE-weighted attendance; zero denominator returns BLANK.
			DIVIDE([Present Records]+[Late Records]+[Half Day Records],[Attendance Records])
		formatString: 0.0%
