	/// Prior-year new hires over dates equivalent to the effective current interval. Calculation: Shift selected start and capped end back 12 months with EDATE; remove existing date filters and evaluate New Hires over that inclusive interval. Purpose: Prevents comparing an incomplete current year with a full prior year. Unit: Count of the population described; displayed as an integer. Date/filter context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications. Empty/zero behavior: Explicit BLANK guards and suppressed totals are retained exactly as written. Limitations: Disjoint dates: previous windows span shifted min/max while current exit/transaction rows retain selected dates. EDATE handles month-end adjustments. Other filters remain; future-only current windows return BLANK. Interpretation: Prior-year baseline for the same effective month/day endpoints.
	measure 'New Hires Prior Equivalent Period' =
			// Prior-year new hires over dates equivalent to the effective current interval.
			// Why: Prevents comparing an incomplete current year with a full prior year.
			// Logic: Shift selected start and capped end back 12 months with EDATE; remove existing date filters and evaluate New Hires over that inclusive interval.
			// Context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications.
			// Empty/zero: Explicit BLANK guards and suppressed totals are retained exactly as written.
			// Unit: Count of the population described; displayed as an integer.
			// Caveat: Disjoint dates: previous windows span shifted min/max while current exit/transaction rows retain selected dates. EDATE handles month-end adjustments. Other filters remain; future-only current windows return BLANK.
			VAR _s=[Period Start Date] VAR _e=[Period End Date] VAR _ps=EDATE(_s,-12) VAR _pe=EDATE(_e,-12) RETURN IF(_s>_e,BLANK(),CALCULATE([New Hires],REMOVEFILTERS('Dim_Date'),DATESBETWEEN('Dim_Date'[Date],_ps,_pe)))
		formatString: #,##0
		displayFolder: 01 Workforce
		lineageTag: 23d67e8d-fa9a-4bd3-8e65-c03b7a173f17

	/// Relative year-over-year change in new hires against the prior equivalent interval. Calculation: (New Hires - New Hires Prior Equivalent Period) / New Hires Prior Equivalent Period. Purpose: Scales the difference by a compatible prior-year baseline. Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place. Date/filter context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications. Empty/zero behavior: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Limitations: Zero or BLANK prior baseline returns BLANK. The prior interval is capped-equivalent, while the current base retains its documented date behavior. Interpretation: Positive means an increase and negative a decrease; desirability depends on the business metric.
	measure 'New Hires YoY Change' =
			// Relative year-over-year change in new hires against the prior equivalent interval.
			// Why: Scales the difference by a compatible prior-year baseline.
			// Logic: (New Hires - New Hires Prior Equivalent Period) / New Hires Prior Equivalent Period.
			// Context: Calendar min/max define explicit Employee Hire/Exit lifecycle windows, capped at global payroll month end. Dim_Date does not directly filter Employee. Department and employee filters apply using extract classifications.
			// Empty/zero: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied.
			// Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place.
			// Caveat: Zero or BLANK prior baseline returns BLANK. The prior interval is capped-equivalent, while the current base retains its documented date behavior.
			DIVIDE([New Hires]-[New Hires Prior Equivalent Period],[New Hires Prior Equivalent Period])
