			// Context: Active Payroll Period, represented by month start, selects employee-month transactions. Department and employee filters apply. Explicit prior/latest/rolling comparisons replace calendar filters as stated in their calculation.
			// Empty/zero: Explicit BLANK guards and suppressed totals are retained exactly as written.
			// Unit: Unspecified source monetary units.
			// Caveat: Disjoint dates: previous windows span shifted min/max while current exit/transaction rows retain selected dates. EDATE handles month-end adjustments. Other filters remain; future-only current windows return BLANK.
			VAR _s=[Period Start Date] VAR _e=[Period End Date] VAR _ps=EDATE(_s,-12) VAR _pe=EDATE(_e,-12) RETURN IF(_s>_e,BLANK(),CALCULATE([Gross Payroll],REMOVEFILTERS('Dim_Date'),DATESBETWEEN('Dim_Date'[Date],_ps,_pe)))
		formatString: #,##0.00
		displayFolder: 04 Payroll
		lineageTag: 2cef19b4-1ce8-4e5f-bbfc-a5a69d999f62

	/// Relative year-over-year change in gross payroll against the prior equivalent interval. Calculation: (Gross Payroll - Gross Payroll Prior Equivalent Period) / Gross Payroll Prior Equivalent Period. Purpose: Scales the difference by a compatible prior-year baseline. Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place. Date/filter context: Active Payroll Period, represented by month start, selects employee-month transactions. Department and employee filters apply. Explicit prior/latest/rolling comparisons replace calendar filters as stated in their calculation. Empty/zero behavior: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Limitations: Zero or BLANK prior baseline returns BLANK. The prior interval is capped-equivalent, while the current base retains its documented date behavior. Interpretation: Positive means an increase and negative a decrease; desirability depends on the business metric.
	measure 'Gross Payroll YoY Change' =
			// Relative year-over-year change in gross payroll against the prior equivalent interval.
			// Why: Scales the difference by a compatible prior-year baseline.
			// Logic: (Gross Payroll - Gross Payroll Prior Equivalent Period) / Gross Payroll Prior Equivalent Period.
			// Context: Active Payroll Period, represented by month start, selects employee-month transactions. Department and employee filters apply. Explicit prior/latest/rolling comparisons replace calendar filters as stated in their calculation.
			// Empty/zero: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied.
			// Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place.
			// Caveat: Zero or BLANK prior baseline returns BLANK. The prior interval is capped-equivalent, while the current base retains its documented date behavior.
			DIVIDE([Gross Payroll]-[Gross Payroll Prior Equivalent Period],[Gross Payroll Prior Equivalent Period])
		formatString: 0.0%
		displayFolder: 04 Payroll
		lineageTag: 199819e0-4553-4b06-b42f-9fccab313d0f

	/// Prior-year applications over dates equivalent to the effective current interval. Calculation: Shift selected start and capped end back 12 months with EDATE; remove existing date filters and evaluate Applications over that inclusive interval. Purpose: Prevents comparing an incomplete current year with a full prior year. Unit: Count of the population described; displayed as an integer. Date/filter context: Active Application Date selects the application cohort; Department applies. Employee job, grade and demographics do not filter recruitment. Outcome statuses are the current extract snapshot. Empty/zero behavior: Explicit BLANK guards and suppressed totals are retained exactly as written. Limitations: Disjoint dates: previous windows span shifted min/max while current exit/transaction rows retain selected dates. EDATE handles month-end adjustments. Other filters remain; future-only current windows return BLANK. Interpretation: Prior-year baseline for the same effective month/day endpoints.
	measure 'Applications Prior Equivalent Period' =
			// Prior-year applications over dates equivalent to the effective current interval.
			// Why: Prevents comparing an incomplete current year with a full prior year.
			// Logic: Shift selected start and capped end back 12 months with EDATE; remove existing date filters and evaluate Applications over that inclusive interval.
			// Context: Active Application Date selects the application cohort; Department applies. Employee job, grade and demographics do not filter recruitment. Outcome statuses are the current extract snapshot.
			// Empty/zero: Explicit BLANK guards and suppressed totals are retained exactly as written.
			// Unit: Count of the population described; displayed as an integer.
			// Caveat: Disjoint dates: previous windows span shifted min/max while current exit/transaction rows retain selected dates. EDATE handles month-end adjustments. Other filters remain; future-only current windows return BLANK.
			VAR _s=[Period Start Date] VAR _e=[Period End Date] VAR _ps=EDATE(_s,-12) VAR _pe=EDATE(_e,-12) RETURN IF(_s>_e,BLANK(),CALCULATE([Applications],REMOVEFILTERS('Dim_Date'),DATESBETWEEN('Dim_Date'[Date],_ps,_pe)))
		formatString: #,##0
		displayFolder: 05 Recruitment
		lineageTag: 7f743286-1a60-4f10-a65e-52cbf2863b62

	/// Relative year-over-year change in applications against the prior equivalent interval. Calculation: (Applications - Applications Prior Equivalent Period) / Applications Prior Equivalent Period. Purpose: Scales the difference by a compatible prior-year baseline. Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place. Date/filter context: Active Application Date selects the application cohort; Department applies. Employee job, grade and demographics do not filter recruitment. Outcome statuses are the current extract snapshot. Empty/zero behavior: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Limitations: Zero or BLANK prior baseline returns BLANK. The prior interval is capped-equivalent, while the current base retains its documented date behavior. Interpretation: Positive means an increase and negative a decrease; desirability depends on the business metric.
	measure 'Applications YoY Change' =
			// Relative year-over-year change in applications against the prior equivalent interval.
			// Why: Scales the difference by a compatible prior-year baseline.
			// Logic: (Applications - Applications Prior Equivalent Period) / Applications Prior Equivalent Period.
			// Context: Active Application Date selects the application cohort; Department applies. Employee job, grade and demographics do not filter recruitment. Outcome statuses are the current extract snapshot.
			// Empty/zero: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied.
			// Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place.
			// Caveat: Zero or BLANK prior baseline returns BLANK. The prior interval is capped-equivalent, while the current base retains its documented date behavior.
