	/// Gross payroll for the complete month immediately before the capped selected endpoint month. Calculation: Use EOMONTH to find prior month start/end, remove existing date filters, and calculate Gross Payroll in that month. Purpose: Supplies a clearly defined one-month comparison to Gross Payroll Latest Month. Unit: Unspecified source monetary units. Date/filter context: Active Payroll Period, represented by month start, selects employee-month transactions. Department and employee filters apply. Explicit prior/latest/rolling comparisons replace calendar filters as stated in their calculation. Empty/zero behavior: Existing DAX scalar and arithmetic BLANK behavior is preserved; no new empty-result substitution is added. Limitations: Other employee/department filters remain. No explicit future-only start guard; endpoint is capped. Currency unspecified. Interpretation: Prior-month monetary baseline; it is not the previous full selected interval.
	measure 'Gross Payroll Previous Month' =
			// Gross payroll for the complete month immediately before the capped selected endpoint month.
			// Why: Supplies a clearly defined one-month comparison to Gross Payroll Latest Month.
			// Logic: Use EOMONTH to find prior month start/end, remove existing date filters, and calculate Gross Payroll in that month.
			// Context: Active Payroll Period, represented by month start, selects employee-month transactions. Department and employee filters apply. Explicit prior/latest/rolling comparisons replace calendar filters as stated in their calculation.
			// Empty/zero: Existing DAX scalar and arithmetic BLANK behavior is preserved; no new empty-result substitution is added.
			// Unit: Unspecified source monetary units.
			// Caveat: Other employee/department filters remain. No explicit future-only start guard; endpoint is capped. Currency unspecified.
			VAR _e=[Period End Date] VAR _s=EOMONTH(_e,-2)+1 VAR _p=EOMONTH(_e,-1) RETURN CALCULATE([Gross Payroll],REMOVEFILTERS('Dim_Date'),DATESBETWEEN('Dim_Date'[Date],_s,_p))
		formatString: #,##0.00
		displayFolder: 04 Payroll
		lineageTag: eeb47f9c-c32b-4197-99ba-86baedb43f29

	/// Gross payroll in the month containing the capped selected endpoint. Calculation: Replace date filters with dates from first of endpoint month through Period End Date, then evaluate Gross Payroll. Purpose: Extracts a single current comparison month from a wider selection. Unit: Unspecified source monetary units. Date/filter context: Active Payroll Period, represented by month start, selects employee-month transactions. Department and employee filters apply. Explicit prior/latest/rolling comparisons replace calendar filters as stated in their calculation. Empty/zero behavior: Existing DAX scalar and arithmetic BLANK behavior is preserved; no new empty-result substitution is added. Limitations: Payroll Period is month start, so selected endpoint determines inclusion of the whole recorded monthly row. Currency unspecified. Interpretation: Payroll-period source amount for the endpoint month, not total selected-period payroll.
	measure 'Gross Payroll Latest Month' =
			// Gross payroll in the month containing the capped selected endpoint.
			// Why: Extracts a single current comparison month from a wider selection.
			// Logic: Replace date filters with dates from first of endpoint month through Period End Date, then evaluate Gross Payroll.
			// Context: Active Payroll Period, represented by month start, selects employee-month transactions. Department and employee filters apply. Explicit prior/latest/rolling comparisons replace calendar filters as stated in their calculation.
			// Empty/zero: Existing DAX scalar and arithmetic BLANK behavior is preserved; no new empty-result substitution is added.
			// Unit: Unspecified source monetary units.
			// Caveat: Payroll Period is month start, so selected endpoint determines inclusion of the whole recorded monthly row. Currency unspecified.
			VAR _e=[Period End Date] VAR _s=DATE(YEAR(_e),MONTH(_e),1) RETURN CALCULATE([Gross Payroll],REMOVEFILTERS('Dim_Date'),DATESBETWEEN('Dim_Date'[Date],_s,_e))
		formatString: #,##0.00
		displayFolder: 04 Payroll
		lineageTag: b3e00115-f8f0-49eb-8063-9ae41e713773

	/// Relative change between latest endpoint-month and immediately preceding month gross payroll. Calculation: (Gross Payroll Latest Month - Gross Payroll Previous Month) / Gross Payroll Previous Month. Purpose: Compares equivalent monthly transaction periods rather than a long interval with a month. Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place. Date/filter context: Active Payroll Period, represented by month start, selects employee-month transactions. Department and employee filters apply. Explicit prior/latest/rolling comparisons replace calendar filters as stated in their calculation. Empty/zero behavior: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied. Limitations: Zero or BLANK previous month returns BLANK; current endpoint is capped, currency unspecified. Interpretation: Positive means month-on-month gross payroll growth; investigate mix, hiring and compensation before judging.
	measure 'Gross Payroll MoM Change' =
			// Relative change between latest endpoint-month and immediately preceding month gross payroll.
			// Why: Compares equivalent monthly transaction periods rather than a long interval with a month.
			// Logic: (Gross Payroll Latest Month - Gross Payroll Previous Month) / Gross Payroll Previous Month.
			// Context: Active Payroll Period, represented by month start, selects employee-month transactions. Department and employee filters apply. Explicit prior/latest/rolling comparisons replace calendar filters as stated in their calculation.
			// Empty/zero: DIVIDE returns BLANK for a zero or BLANK denominator; a BLANK numerator also stays BLANK even with a positive denominator. No alternate result is supplied.
			// Unit: Ratio stored as a fraction; displayed as a percentage with one decimal place.
			// Caveat: Zero or BLANK previous month returns BLANK; current endpoint is capped, currency unspecified.
			DIVIDE([Gross Payroll Latest Month]-[Gross Payroll Previous Month],[Gross Payroll Previous Month])
		formatString: 0.0%
		displayFolder: 04 Payroll
		lineageTag: e6929475-4454-441c-b7db-088129b91b47

	/// Gross payroll over the trailing 12-month window ending at the capped endpoint. Calculation: Remove current calendar filters and evaluate Gross Payroll with DATESINPERIOD(endpoint, -12, MONTH). Purpose: Smooths individual-month effects using an explicit trailing window. Unit: Unspecified source monetary units. Date/filter context: Active Payroll Period, represented by month start, selects employee-month transactions. Department and employee filters apply. Explicit prior/latest/rolling comparisons replace calendar filters as stated in their calculation. Empty/zero behavior: Existing DAX scalar and arithmetic BLANK behavior is preserved; no new empty-result substitution is added. Limitations: Early source periods may have fewer than 12 observed months; not annualized. Other filters remain; currency unspecified. Interpretation: Source monetary amount over the available rolling-year period.
	measure 'Gross Payroll Rolling 12 Months' =
			// Gross payroll over the trailing 12-month window ending at the capped endpoint.
			// Why: Smooths individual-month effects using an explicit trailing window.
			// Logic: Remove current calendar filters and evaluate Gross Payroll with DATESINPERIOD(endpoint, -12, MONTH).
			// Context: Active Payroll Period, represented by month start, selects employee-month transactions. Department and employee filters apply. Explicit prior/latest/rolling comparisons replace calendar filters as stated in their calculation.
			// Empty/zero: Existing DAX scalar and arithmetic BLANK behavior is preserved; no new empty-result substitution is added.
			// Unit: Unspecified source monetary units.
			// Caveat: Early source periods may have fewer than 12 observed months; not annualized. Other filters remain; currency unspecified.
			VAR _e=[Period End Date] RETURN CALCULATE([Gross Payroll],REMOVEFILTERS('Dim_Date'),DATESINPERIOD('Dim_Date'[Date],_e,-12,MONTH))
		formatString: #,##0.00
		displayFolder: 04 Payroll
		lineageTag: 8d2a032e-231e-4022-bbea-c6612de82c09

	/// Readable workforce snapshot title containing the capped as-of date. Calculation: Concatenate Workforce as of with Period End Date formatted dd MMM yyyy. Purpose: Keeps the snapshot endpoint visible when date filters change. Unit: Text. Date/filter context: Current Dim_Date selection; endpoint is capped where referenced. Department and employee selections do not change the global coverage cutoff. Empty/zero behavior: Existing DAX scalar and arithmetic BLANK behavior is preserved; no new empty-result substitution is added. Limitations: Text only; does not itself filter or validate the selected interval. Interpretation: Read as the endpoint used by lifecycle metrics.
	measure 'Dynamic Workforce Title' =
			// Readable workforce snapshot title containing the capped as-of date.
			// Why: Keeps the snapshot endpoint visible when date filters change.
			// Logic: Concatenate Workforce as of with Period End Date formatted dd MMM yyyy.
			// Context: Current Dim_Date selection; endpoint is capped where referenced. Department and employee selections do not change the global coverage cutoff.
			// Empty/zero: Existing DAX scalar and arithmetic BLANK behavior is preserved; no new empty-result substitution is added.
			// Unit: Text.
			// Caveat: Text only; does not itself filter or validate the selected interval.
			"Workforce as of " & FORMAT([Period End Date],"dd MMM yyyy")
		formatString: @
		displayFolder: 00 Context
		lineageTag: 6c33ea3b-c19a-40c8-8a63-e99b68fffca5

